From: stephan-xyz <stephan@zehrer.xyz>
Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 16:20:08 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 53/53] testnetd: fake network adapter with a DHCP server, for
 netstack tests

testnetd registers network.test0 (or the scheme given as argument) with
one host behind it, 10.0.9.1, that answers ARP, ping and DHCP (offers
10.0.9.2/24). It counts DHCP messages for other MACs and packets with a
source outside 10.0.9.0/24 in /tmp/testnetd.log. Started from a shell
it re-runs itself as a daemon.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
